title: Pass response headers and fieldValidation through, so Kubernetes::REST on_warning
  and field_validation reach the async client
updated: 2026-11-06T21:17:09Z
---

Kubernetes::REST 1.111 (local tree, master d8707a2) adds on_warning (a coderef that check_response calls for every Warning header) and field_validation / a per-call fieldValidation option on create, update, update_status, patch and patch_status. Both need the request path to cooperate: check_response reads Warning headers from Kubernetes::REST::HTTPResponse->headers (hashref, lower-cased name to arrayref of values), which the async client does not fill when it builds the HTTPResponse, and fieldValidation is a query parameter the async client has to send on its own write path. Today neither reaches Net::Async::Kubernetes: no warnings are delivered, and fieldValidation is not sent. Done = the async client builds HTTPResponse with headers (on_warning fires, a test with a Warning: 299 - "text" response), passes field_validation / fieldValidation through like the sync client, and the POD says so. Pin Kubernetes::REST to the version that has on_warning. Not part of the 2026-11-06 release round.
